Review: rn-y594 epic end (xhigh), range 6bac0db..f60441a, worktree .worktrees/rn-y594
Command: Skill(code-review, "xhigh --fix /home/coder/workspace/isekai/.worktrees/rn-y594"). It ran, but its edits were refused by the hook (rule 2), so nothing was applied. The reviewer's words follow unchanged.

--- reviewer's words ---

I reviewed the rn-y594 diff and found 10 issues, but none of the fixes were applied. The repo's PreToolUse hook refused both edits to `src/sprite/store.rs` ("Rule 2 — Pick something up before you change the repository": this session holds no work in the rn-y594 worktree). The hook pointed me to the rn-6ptr worktree instead, but that belongs to a different epic, so I didn't edit there and didn't try to get around the hook another way. The worktree is still clean.

The diff only adds 9 doc-comment lines to `write_atomic` and `publish_new` (from `milestone/rn-pzbl` 6bac0db to f60441a). I checked them against the code, the human's decision (B: no parent-directory sync), the confirmed spec note in rn-y594.8q9 and the epic's "약속" section. The function bodies, `stage_bytes`, `Staged`, `NEXT_TEMP`, `StoreError` and `Cargo.lock` are unchanged. No CLAUDE.md applies to these files, so the conventions check found nothing.

```json
[
  {
    "file": "src/sprite/store.rs",
    "line": 157,
    "summary": "The new first line of the write_atomic doc promises atomic replacement on every platform, but the epic says guarantees may only be stated for Linux, and rn-y594.8q9 lists Windows, macOS, Emscripten and network mounts as unconfirmed.",
    "failure_scenario": "Someone reads the rustdoc and relies on readers never seeing a partial file on Windows (MoveFileExW fallback, not documented as atomic) or on NFS/SMB (rename(2) BUGS: it can report failure after taking effect). The comment turns a 'not verified' entry into a promise, which the 2lf review focus says to reject."
  },
